@startuml UC-SUBTASK-UPDATE
' UC-27.3 - Update Subtask | semantic key: UC-SUBTASK-UPDATE
' Source: data/use_cases/sprint-work/UC-SUBTASK-UPDATE.yml
' Business Rules: BR-SPRINT-TASK-ACTIVE-SPRINT, BR-SPRINT-TASK-DEVELOPER, BR-SUBTASK-SINGLE-LEVEL
' Trace comments ' [ref] name the YAML element behind the next action.
' No title: the Word caption supplies it.
' One Activity Final shared by all paths (team decision 2026-10-06; UML allows one or several). It
' is reached after the changes are saved (postconditions met) or with the subtask unchanged (EX-01
' rejection, AF-01 cancellation).
' Layout (2026-10-06): the decision "Submit changes?" is drawn in the System lane, where the System
' waits for the Developer's answer; the guards name the Developer's choice. In the Developer lane
' its merge forced a detour across the lanes. The final stays in the System lane.
!include ../../_shared/activity-style.puml
|DEV| $lane_title("Developer")
|SYS| $lane_title("System")

|DEV|
start
' [NF1, BR-SPRINT-TASK-DEVELOPER]
:Open subtask for editing;
|SYS|
' [NF2]
:Display current
editable values;
if ($question("Submit changes?")) then ($guard_left("[submit]"))
  |DEV|
  ' [NF3]
  :Revise information
  and submit subtask;
  |SYS|
  ' [NF4]
  :Validate subtask changes;
  if ($question("Parent still in active Sprint?")) then ($guard_left("[in active Sprint]"))
    ' [NF4, POST1]
    :Save subtask changes;
    if ($question("Parent progress affected?")) then ($guard_left("[affected]"))
      ' [POST2]
      :Recalculate parent-task progress;
    else ($guard_right("[not", "affected]"))
    endif
  else ($guard_right("[no longer in", "active Sprint — EX-01]"))
    ' [EX-01, BR-SPRINT-TASK-ACTIVE-SPRINT, GUIDE-7.3]
    :Reject subtask update;
  endif
else ($guard_right("[cancel", "editing — AF-01]"))
  |SYS|
  ' [AF-01.1]
  :Keep subtask
  unchanged;
endif
|SYS|
stop
@enduml
